      "body": "## Overview\n\nKeep the latest 1024 samples per token count, compute the rolling median, and label the logged count as window_count. Wire the regression test into engine CI.\n\nDraft/WIP: focused regressions have been validated; human review and the remaining checks below are pending before this is ready.\n\n## Claims\n\nKeep the latest 1024 samples per token count, compute the rolling median, and label the logged count as window_count. Wire the regression test into engine CI.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidated on a remote Ubuntu x86_64 machine with Ryzen 9 9900X, Python 3.12.13 and PyTorch 2.13.0+cpu, against base `698e79f3bdbbe4fe7d6be6d91b358a7f430753ab`.\n\n```sh\nTRITON_DEFAULT_BACKEND=cpu VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 PYTHONPATH=. ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_forward_context.py --confcutdir=tests -q\n```\n\nBaseline: 1 failed. Patched: 1 passed.\n\nApplicable pre-commit checks passed. Upstream CI has not yet been evaluated for this draft.\n\n## Details\n\nApplies when VLLM_LOG_BATCHSIZE_INTERVAL enables optional timing diagnostics. The median becomes a rolling median over at most 1024 samples per token count. The regression is wired into engine CI.\n\nAI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used for analysis, implementation and validation. The submitter's human review remains pending.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Scoped to the reported contract and reuses existing behavior where possible.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Focused tests passed; remaining validation and human review are described above.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Applicable pre-commit checks passed.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Scope, evidence and limitations are recorded.\n</details>\n",
